  <artifactId>agents-tools</artifactId>
  <name>agents-tools</name>
  <description>
    The agent tool layer: AgentToolProvider and the tool resolvers, tool
    sources, the tool guard and governance chain, the MCP connection manager
    (DynamicMcpConnectionManager and friends), the MCP registry, MCP Apps and
    MCP review, and the built-in tools (code, openapi, script, messaging,
    device, x402, e2b, commerce, search, audio, tables, capability,
    documentgen, media), plus the data tables feature (com.agenticai.core.tables).
    Split out of core/agents by ADR-0023; the Java packages are unchanged.

    Direction: agents-tools depends on agents and agents-turn, never the reverse.
    The kernel and the turn path reach tools through ports agents owns:
    tools.AgentToolPort (implemented by AgentToolProvider), tools.ToolReplaySafety
    (AgentToolGovernance) and the tools.ToolSearchToolNames constants. Shared
    tool vocabulary the kernel and the turn path use directly stays in agents:
    step events, the tool-call log, the step and effect journals, tool
    classification and trifecta enforcement, the sandbox file registry and
    sandbox client, and the ports other modules implement
    (WebToolPort, BrowserToolPort, the messaging ports, ScheduleTaskToolFactory,
    CodingTaskToolFactory).
  </description>

